{
  "Motif": "elves",
  "Name": "Elves",
  "Draw": "Elves are tall, slim and very still. Long limbs, narrow faces, high cheekbones, swept pointed ears, and long hair bound back. Their gear is grown rather than forged - layered cloth and soft leather cut in leaf shapes, bark and living wood worked into bowstaves and hilts, silver used only as fine line detail. Nothing about them is bulky and nothing about them is hurried.",
  "ElementDraw": {
    "fire": "The cloth is burnt autumn at every hem and smoking faintly, embers are caught in the hair, and the wood of their gear is edged hot orange as though lit along the grain.",
    "ice": "Frost forms along the folds of the cloth and down the bowstring, the hair is stiff with rime, and the skin has gone bloodless white. Pale blue light and visible breath.",
    "lightning": "The hair lifts and floats, arcs run the length of the stave and the arrow, and every silver line on the gear flickers yellow.",
    "earth": "Moss and lichen have grown into the cloth, bark has thickened over the forearms, and root and green thread run through the hair. The wood of their weapons is still alive.",
    "arcane": "Violet light along every silver line and inside the eyes, and the outline of the figure is faintly doubled, as though it is standing slightly to one side of itself."
  },
  "ValidFloors": [
    3,
    8
  ],
